===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*haliþaz||man, hero}}, further etymology unknown.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|helid}} ({{cog|de|Held}}), {{cog|osx|helid}}, {{cog|odt|helt}} ({{cog|nl|held}}), {{cog|fy|held}}, {{cog|non|halr}}, {{m|non|hǫlðr}} ({{cog|no|hold}}, {{cog|sv|hjälte}}). The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|κέλωρ}}, {{cog|txb||kālyśke|boy}}.

